  <x:String x:Key="remoteSupport.launchButton">Launch AnyDesk</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="remoteSupport.downloadButton">Download AnyDesk</x:String>
  <!-- 2026-10-05: кнопка «Скопировать информацию об устройстве» (DeviceInfoReport) -->
  <x:String x:Key="remoteSupport.copyDeviceInfo">Copy device information</x:String>

  <!-- Knowledge base -->
  <x:String x:Key="kb.subtitle">Answers to common questions about running the till. Click a question to see the answer.</x:String>

  <x:String x:Key="kb.catFeaturesTitle">App features</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.offlineQ">Can I work offline?</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.offlineA">Yes. The till keeps ringing up sales offline — receipts are saved locally and sent to the server automatically as soon as the connection is restored. The number of receipts waiting to be sent is shown in the status bar at the bottom of the screen.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.deferredCartsQ">What are "Held carts"?</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.deferredCartsA">Lets you put the current receipt on hold (for example, if the customer has stepped away to get money) and come back to it later without losing the items in the cart. Opens from the side menu.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.themesQ">Can I change how the till looks?</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.themesA">Yes — in "Marketplace" → "Themes" you can pick a ready-made theme or set your own accent color, font and corner rounding. Some themes are paid: 2 are free (Gold, Blue), and the rest are unlocked with a serial number.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.zeroStockQ">What if a product is out of stock but the customer wants to buy it?</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.zeroStockA">When you add a product with zero stock, the till shows a warning and asks you to confirm the sale — after confirming, enter how much to add to stock. The stock updates automatically and the sale goes through as usual.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.irregularReceiptsQ">What are "Irregular receipts"?</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.irregularReceiptsA">A section in the side menu that automatically collects receipts that did not go through normally: sales at zero stock, server upload errors, receipts still uploading. Useful for reconciliation at the end of a shift.</x:String>

  <x:String x:Key="kb.catCashierTitle">How the cashier role works and what it can access</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.permissionsQ">What permissions can a cashier be given?</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.permissionsA">Permissions are granted to each employee separately in NurCRM (the web panel): access to till settings, scales, price tags, discounts, price changes, removing items from the cart, warehouse/purchasing, suppliers, returns, sales (reports) and shifts. Sections without permission are hidden or unavailable in the till menu.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.financeAccessQ">Why can't the cashier see "Finance" or "Sales"?</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.financeAccessA">These sections are available only to employees with the matching permission ("Sales", etc.) granted in NurCRM. If a section is not visible, this employee has not been granted that permission.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.shiftQ">How do I open/close a shift?</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.shiftA">The "Open shift"/"Close shift" buttons are on the top bar of the till. Open a shift before the first sale of the day and close it at the end of the day — on closing, the till shows a revenue report and the cash balance.</x:String>

  <x:String x:Key="kb.catUpdatesTitle">How to update the app</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.checkUpdateQ">How do I know if there's a new version of the till?</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.checkUpdateA">The till checks for updates automatically on every launch. To check manually, go to Settings → Updates → "Check for updates"; if a new version is found, the "Update" button appears there too.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.rollbackQ">Can I roll back to an earlier version if something breaks after an update?</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.rollbackA">Yes — Settings → Updates has a list of previous versions, and you can roll back to any of them.</x:String>

  <x:String x:Key="kb.catFailureTitle">What to do if something goes wrong, and who to contact</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.errorDialogQ">The till showed an error window — what should I do?</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.errorDialogA">The error window has 2 buttons: "Close" simply closes the window, and "Defer error" logs the error (see "Logs and errors") so you can keep working as if nothing happened. Use "Defer error" if the error doesn't stop you from working right now.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.logsQ">Where can I see what happened during a failure?</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.logsA">Side menu → "Logs and errors" shows recent warnings, errors and server disconnects. The "Open logs folder" button opens the folder with detailed technical files, which you can send to support.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.remoteSupportQ">How do I get remote help from NurCRM support?</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.remoteSupportA">Side menu → "NurCRM support" → "Launch AnyDesk". A connection address (ID) will appear — read it to the support agent by phone or on WhatsApp so they can connect to your computer and help.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.printerQ">The till doesn't see a receipt printer connected via USB — what should I do?</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="kb.q.printerA">In Settings → Printing, click "Find" again (the list doesn't refresh on its own). If the printer was set up with Zadig and still doesn't appear, reconnect it and try again, or contact support via "NurCRM support".</x:String>
