    <!-- 2026-09-29: галочка теперь значит «постоянный PLU за товаром», а не «подряд по списку». -->
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.scales.sequentialPlu">Fixed PLU per product</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.scales.sequentialPluTip">Each product gets its PLU number once and keeps it on every send: adding products, search, filters and sorting do not change it. A new product gets the lowest free number starting from “Start PLU”. You can correct the number in the PLU column — on the next send the till writes the product to the new slot, clears the old one and moves the scale keys to the new number. Untick to take the PLU from the product card on the website.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.scales.webPlu">PLU as on the website</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.scales.webPluTip">The scale slot number = the product's PLU on the website. The till gives ticked weighed goods without a PLU free numbers on the website — website, till and scale match.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.scales.directLan">Directly via cable</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.scales.directLanTip">The till talks to the scale directly over the local network, without the server. Not tested on real scales — check the port in the scale's system menu.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.scales.lanSettings">Connection settings…</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.scales.lanSettingsTip">The scale's address, port and password are in a separate window, along with a connection test.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.tgSetup.title">Connect the Telegram bot</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.tgSetup.intro">The bot sends you a summary of each closed shift and answers commands: revenue, top products, what to reorder, debtors. It works right from the store: no server of your own and no public IP address needed.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.tgSetup.warning">The bot itself is created by Telegram, not by the till: BotFather has no API, so step 1 is done manually in Telegram. The till will take care of everything else.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.tgSetup.step1">Step 1. Create a bot with @BotFather</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.tgSetup.step1Body">Click “Open BotFather” — a chat opens in Telegram. Send the /newbot command there, then choose a name and a username for the bot (the username must end in “bot”). BotFather will reply with a token — a long string like 123456789:AAG...</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.tgSetup.openBotFather">Open BotFather</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.tgSetup.copyNewBot">Copy /newbot</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.tgSetup.step2">Step 2. Paste the token</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.tgSetup.step2Body">Copy the token from the chat with BotFather and paste it here in full. The till will check it and show the bot's name.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.tgSetup.checkToken">Check token</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.tgSetup.pasteToken">Paste from clipboard</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.tgSetup.step3">Step 3. Send “Start” to your bot</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.tgSetup.step3Body">Telegram doesn't let a bot write first — you need to open your bot and press “Start” first. After that, the till will know which chat to send summaries to.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.tgSetup.openMyBot">Open my bot</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.tgSetup.detect">Detect recipient</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.tgSetup.step4">Step 4. Test and turn on</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.tgSetup.sendTest">Send a test message</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.tgSetup.summaryOnClose">Send a summary when a shift is closed</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.tgSetup.answerCommands">Reply to commands in Telegram</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.tgSetup.commandsHelp">Commands: /segodnya — today's revenue, /nedelya — revenue for the week, /top — top products, /abc — ABC analysis, /sezon — seasonality, /soveti — recommendations, /zakaz — what to reorder, /ostatki — what's running out, /dolgi — debtors. The bot replies while the till is on.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.tgSetup.done">Done</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.sales.excelTip">Export sales and stock analytics for the selected period to Excel, with charts.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.sales.wordTip">Export the same report to Word, with tables and charts.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.sales.metricsTab">Metrics</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.finance.excelTip">Export analytics for the selected period to Excel, with charts and ABC analysis.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.finance.wordTip">The same report in Word — tables, charts and ABC analysis.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.finance.expenses">Expenses (cash out)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.finance.profitAfterExpenses">Profit after expenses</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.zeroMoney">0.00 som</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.voice.title">Voice control test</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.voice.howTo">How to use</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.voice.howToBody">Always start with the keyword «касса», followed right away by the command — the microphone is always listening, so there's no button to press.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.voice.exRu1">• «касса картошка два килограмма» — adds 2 kg of potatoes to the receipt</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.voice.exRu2">• «касса молоко» — adds 1 pc of milk (no number means 1)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.voice.exRu3">• «касса манго 20 штук» — if the product has a per-piece price, adds it by the piece right away, without asking</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.voice.exRu4">• «касса манго 2 пачки» — adds whole packs right away; if you say just a number without «штук»/«пачки», it will ask you to clarify</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.voice.exRu5">• «касса найди сахар» — finds and shows the product without adding it</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.voice.exRu6">• «касса убери последнюю» — removes the last added item (asks for confirmation)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.voice.exRu7">• «касса очисти чек» — clears the whole receipt (asks for confirmation)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.voice.exRu8">• «касса повтори» — repeats the last product added</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.voice.exRu9">• «касса оплата» — goes to payment for the receipt</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.voice.exRu10">• «касса отмена» — cancels the current operation</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.voice.kyHeader">Kyrgyz commands (Кыргызча буйруктар)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.voice.kyNote">Kyrgyz commands are recognized better when the language is set to Kyrgyz (Settings → Screen) — the till then uses a model trained on Kyrgyz.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.voice.exKy1">• «касса нан эки даана» — adds 2 pcs of bread to the receipt</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.voice.exKy2">• «касса сүт» — adds 1 pc of milk (no number means 1)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.voice.exKy3">• «касса кант тап» — finds and shows the product without adding it</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.voice.exKy4">• «касса акыркысын өчүр» — removes the last added item (asks for confirmation)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.voice.exKy5">• «касса чекти тазала» — clears the whole receipt (asks for confirmation)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.voice.exKy6">• «касса кайтала» — repeats the last product added</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.voice.exKy7">• «касса төлө» — goes to payment for the receipt</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.voice.exKy8">• «касса жокко чыгар» — cancels the current operation</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.voice.notHeard">Didn't catch it? Try the phrase in the “Check text without a microphone” field below — you'll see how the app parses it, without a microphone and without actually adding anything to the receipt.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.voice.manualTitle">Check text without a microphone</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.voice.manualHint">Type a phrase as if the microphone had already recognized it (with or without the word «касса») — you'll see how the parser handles it.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.voice.parse">Parse</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.voice.lockTitle">Voice lock</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.voice.lockBody">Records the cashier's voice — every voice command is then checked against it. If the voice doesn't match, the command is NOT executed and a warning appears (including a spoken one). This isn't a password: a cold, noise or a different microphone can sometimes cause a false mismatch — just repeat the command or use the mouse/keyboard.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.voice.download">Download module (~27 MB)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.voice.enroll">🎙 Record voice (3 phrases)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.voice.lockOn">Lock on</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.voice.unitsTitle">Unit dictionary</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.voice.unitsBody">Russian and Kyrgyz units are built in (кг, л, шт, даана, бөтөлкө, etc.) — you can add your own here if your store uses others (for example, «мешок», «ящик»). The word is what the cashier will SAY out loud; the abbreviation is only for display in the list.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.voice.unitWordHint">Word, e.g., мешок</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.voice.unitAbbrHint">Abbreviation, e.g., меш</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.voice.aliasTitle">Product training</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.voice.aliasBody">If speech recognition keeps failing to understand a product name (or cashiers call it by a colloquial word that isn't on the product card), link SEVERAL phrases to the product at once (3 or more is best): the more variants of how the name may sound, the more reliable the recognition. One phrase per line — what the cashier will SAY after «касса» (without quantity/unit), for example, «кола» / «кокакола» / «чёрный напиток».</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.voice.aliasProductHint">Product: start typing the name…</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.voice.aliasAdd">Add phrases</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.voice.heardLive">Heard (live)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.owner.voice.recognized">Recognized commands</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.settings.monitor.samplePositions">2 items</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.settings.monitor.sampleQty2">×2 pcs</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.settings.monitor.sampleSum320">320.00 som</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.settings.monitor.sampleQty1">×1 pc</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.settings.monitor.sampleSum95">95.00 som</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.settings.telegram.title">Owner's Telegram bot</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.settings.telegram.desc">You get a summary of each closed shift in Telegram: revenue, receipts, average receipt, cash and cashless, cash in and cash out, shortage or surplus. Works right from the store — no public IP or server of your own needed.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.settings.telegram.wizardButton">Connect the bot (step by step)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.settings.telegram.manualHint">To connect manually: 1) in Telegram, send @BotFather the /newbot command and get a token; 2) paste the token here; 3) open your bot and press “Start”; 4) press “Detect recipient”.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.settings.telegram.tokenLabel">Bot token</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.settings.telegram.detectRecipient">Detect recipient</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.settings.telegram.sendTest">Send test message</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.settings.telegram.summaryOnClose">Send a summary when a shift is closed</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.settings.telegram.answerCommands">Reply to commands in Telegram</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.settings.telegram.commandsHelp">Bot commands: /segodnya — today's revenue, /nedelya — this week's revenue, /top — top products, /abc — ABC analysis, /sezon — seasonality, /soveti — recommendations, /zakaz — what to reorder, /ostatki — what's running low, /dolgi — debtors with a ready WhatsApp link. The bot replies only while the till is on: the app has no server of its own.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.settings.telegram.debtReminders">Send debt reminders</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.settings.telegram.debtRemindersHint">Telegram reminders go only to clients who subscribed to the bot themselves via a personal link (the “Copy link” button in the client card). Telegram doesn't allow messaging people by phone number, so for the other debtors the bot will send you a list with WhatsApp links.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.settings.telegram.ownerPhone">Owner's phone (for replies to messages sent to clients)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.settings.telegram.aiTitle">AI assistant for chatting (free, Google Gemini)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.settings.telegram.aiHint">Even without a key the bot understands plain phrases: “how much did we make today”, “who owes”, “price of cola”. To let it chat freely and give advice, get a free Google key (a Google account is needed, no card) and paste it here. Exact figures are still calculated by the till; the AI only receives a short shop summary. On the free tier Google may use requests to improve its services. Empty field — AI is off.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.settings.telegram.aiGetKey">Get a free key</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.settings.telegram.aiTest">Test AI</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.settings.telegram.groqTitle">Web search for the AI (free, Groq)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.settings.telegram.groqHint">A free Google Gemini key cannot search the web. With a Groq key the AI advisor finds rates, prices and news on the web, and photo search finds product pictures. Press “Get a free key” → sign in with Google → “Create API Key”, copy the key (gsk_…) and paste it here (no card, 1000 requests a day). For search only the question is sent; if Gemini's daily limit runs out, Groq answers itself — then the shop summary is sent too. Empty field — search is off.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.settings.telegram.groqTest">Test search</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.settings.telegram.routerTitle">Backup AI models (free, OpenRouter, optional)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.settings.telegram.routerHint">If Gemini's daily limit runs out, a free OpenRouter model answers (50 requests a day). Press “Get a free key” → sign in with Google → “Create API Key”, copy the key (sk-or-…) and paste it here. The question and the shop summary then go to OpenRouter. Empty field — off.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.settings.dynamicQr.toggle">Show the customer a QR code with the receipt amount</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.settings.dynamicQr.desc">Instead of the bank's regular QR code, the customer display shows a code with the receipt amount already filled in — no need to type it manually. Payment details are taken from the QR code uploaded above.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.settings.dynamicQr.warning">Before turning this on, scan a test receipt with the apps of two or three banks: the format has been checked against MBank's QR code but not tested with other banks. The cashier still confirms the payment manually — the till doesn't detect the payment on its own.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.settings.bank.showAtCheckout">Show at checkout</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.settings.lanScale.title">Network scale (product upload)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.settings.lanScale.desc">The address, port and password are found in the scale's own system menu. The “Scales” window uses the same values when uploading the product list.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.settings.lanScale.ip">Scale IP address</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.settings.lanScale.port">Port</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.settings.lanScale.passwordHint">The password is exactly 4 digits, usually 0030. If it's wrong, the scale blocks access after several attempts: then turn the scale off and on again and enter the correct password. The port is usually 1111.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.settings.lanScale.openDialog">Open connection settings…</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="loc.settings.lanScale.test">Test scale connection</x:String>
    <!-- 2026-09-28: окно «Настройки весов Штрих-ПРИНТ» и штрих-код этикетки весов. -->
    <x:String x:Key="loc.settings.lanScale.deviceSettings">Scale settings (keyboard, label, barcode)…</x:String>
